iews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"sol\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Related capabilities were searched and bounded-surface-residue-transfer@1 was retrieved completely. Its physical function matches, but its implemented applicability is explicitly restricted to surface-21-lin-113 and that surface's creator. It therefore cannot presently execute for Sol on surface-34-sol-201. Develop only the missing explicit applicability binding through the current-conversation development handoff, reusing the existing transfer implementation rather than reinventing it. small-soil-patch-preparation retains residue inside the source boundary; pickup, gather, drop and give do not implement this checked external residue transfer. No transfer, permission, mastery or elapsed world time is granted by this review.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"Implement the smallest Sol-specific applicability extension to bounded-surface-residue-transfer@1, recording code reuse of handler long.residue-transfer and equivalence surface-residue:checked-short-external-transfer:1. Reuse its conservation, geometry, accounting and process checks; do not remove the original instance restriction globally. Explicit new binding: actor sol, source surface-34-sol-201, source center (13,25), source radius 0.2. Depend on the existing live prepared-surface record, residue entries and revisions, visible geometry/occupancy checks, persistent deposits and process ledger. Inspect complete implementation records during development; do not reconstruct omitted source-entry coordinates from the partial observation. No prerequisite skill other than Sol's individual study of the delivered interface; no tools, containers, food or other material inputs are supplied.\\\\nInterface: start(sourceId,destinationX,destinationY), resume(processId), cancel(processId), using exact identities. Start requires sourceId=surface-34-sol-201 and explicitly supplied finite receiver coordinates; never select a receiver automatically. Receiver is a radius-0.1 ground disk, wholly inside world bounds [0,48] by [0,36], with center separation from source greater than 0.3 and at most 0.5. Both centers and every moved portion must remain within 0.65 of Sol. Require actual visible physical access, appropriate occupancy checks, and a visible swept-radius route clear of people, plants, obstacles and unrelated reservations. The visible annotation is not proof of physical clearance. Do not assume access rights or consent from registration; preserve applicable existing ownership/access checks and require independent communication/action from any other participant if needed.\\\\nStudy costs one simulation round and 0.2 energy. A valid fresh start costs one round and 0.5 energy for an actual physical feasibility examination, before any transfer. Invalid identity, binding, coordinates, bounds or range fails before beginning and costs nothing; an examination actually performed but finding blockage consumes its examination time and energy and reports the obstruction without success. A feasible examination creates an exact processId binding actor, source revision and entries, receiver, checked routes and allowance. It permits at most two subsequent attended work rounds, each costing 1 energy and moving at most 0.02 mass, with a total allowance of at most 0.04 actual available residue. Maximum study plus examination plus full work is four rounds and 2.7 energy, excluding travel and any separately requested later examination. Require sufficient energy before each paid step; no debt or free work.\\\\nUse exact integer hundredth-mass accounting. The reported initial live state is zero loose cover and 0.04 residue, not a source of new cover or stock. Resolve and revalidate actual entry masses at execution. Each successful atomic work round subtracts exactly the moved amount from identified source entries and adds that same amount to persistent external nonfood, nonharvestable ground deposits at the selected receiver. Preserve source-entry provenance, source surface identity, deposit identity and moved extents. Retain any unmoved residue and its location. The sum of remaining source residue and its transferred deposits is conserved; unrelated material remains untouched. Do not convert deposits to inventory or food. If the physical handler cannot move a particular entry under its existing constraints, report that limit rather than inventing a tool or mechanism.\\\\nBefore every work charge revalidate visibility, reach, occupancy, source revision, actual remaining entry mass and the swept route. Changed geometry or conflicting revisions pauses before further charges or movement; no unattended work occurs. Persist exact paid progress, remaining per-process allowance, provenance, receiver and successful transfers. Resume requires the same actor and exact processId, revalidates current feasibility and never resets paid progress or allowance. If safe reconciliation is impossible, retain the partial result and require a new paid examination for a new process rather than replaying completed transfers. Interruptions and global pauses preserve committed work and paid effort. Cancel closes the process and releases only its locks; death likewise closes it. Neither restores moved matter nor refunds spent energy/time. There is no material escrow to refund; unspent energy and unmoved matter remain where they actually are. Cancellation and repeated starts cannot reset residue quantities. Any fresh attempt examines live remaining mass and pays a fresh examination. Implement these rules as execution code, not repeated model review.\\\\nProducts are only dated physical findings and actual persistent residue deposits. No background progress, automatic maintenance, disposal or regeneration is introduced; deposits remain physical ground matter under existing world rules. Later displacement or deterioration must be an actual supported world event, never an implicit cleanup. A cleared-looking footprint does not establish suitable soil: grant no planting certification, fertility, moisture, restoration, food, viability guarantee or reward, and do not alter root-placement restrictions. Development/review waiting advances no simulation time.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":1,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Functional displacement is separate from experience. This request, registration, implementation and study award no pleasure or satisfaction. No new reward mechanism or protected-account changes are authorized. Reuse the existing residue-qualified-practice evidence path only for actual personally applicable examined findings or completed legitimate work; verified informative failure may provide evidence, but a query or attempted invocation alone does not. Deduplicate the applicability extension against bounded-surface-residue-transfer by underlying event, source revision and functional outcome, so reuse, resume and renaming cannot double-count. Preserve established executable amount/cap, cooldown and decay rules; if those cannot be established in the development handoff, emit evidence without an experience award rather than inventing one. Familiar legitimate practice need not be novel to qualify under those rules. No physical-comfort increase is specified, the comfort cap remains 10, and nutrition, reward accounts, budgets, goals and permissions remain unchanged.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Reuse the surface-work visual component and existing transfer/deposit renderer metadata rather than claiming a new visual invention. Emit observable examination, blocked, paused, transfer-committed and cancelled events with actor, processId, source/deposit identities, locations, tick, actual moved mass, remaining mass and provenance as applicable. Render persistent deposits with reusable nonfood ground-matter metadata including position, footprint, material/provenance, quantity and actual state; render source changes only after committed subtraction. Show partial progress and obstruction truthfully. Requests, study, infeasible examinations, pauses and incomplete work must not show completed clearing, transfer or planting success. A completed transfer denotes only its actual conserved displacement, not certified soil or restoration. Do not disclose hidden stock, unseen obstructions or concealed resources through visuals.\\\"}]}\"\n}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}],"phase":"final_answer"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":true,"prompt_cache_key":"90742e6e-4499-40dc-9e6a-2025f15be8b4","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"json_schema","name":"bounded_decision","description":null,"schema":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["queries","result_json"],"properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["section","search","ids","offset","part"],"properties":{"section":{"type":"string","enum":["abilities","inventory","knowledge","projects","memory","state","observed"]},"search":{"type":"string","maxLength":400},"ids":{"type":"array","maxItems":4,"items":{"type":"string","maxLength":240}},"offset":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"part":{"type":"integer","minimum":0}}}},"result_json":{"type":["string","null"]}}},"strict":true},"verbosity":"medium"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7041,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens_details":{"ttl_30m_tokens":0,"ttl_12h_tokens":0}},"output_tokens":1619,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":103},"total_tokens":8660,"attribution":{"items":{"msg_099c0880ab6a49f1016b043251837487d184e424659de70fc5":{"input_tokens":6411,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"content":[{"input_tokens":6411,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"out